[Music]  called back to be put on display russian  soldiers rehearsed for victory day the  may 9th anniversary marks russia's  triumph over nazi germany in the second  world war  the day is celebrated across europe  but this year it carries new  significance moscow will look to  highlight victories in ukraine despite  achieving very little  leaving ukraine's president to issue a  warning to obey curfews and air raid  sirens with fear russia could increase  its attacks  those worries a reality on saturday with  strikes in the southern port city of  odessa and across the east  the ground started crumbling the roof  was shaking says this donetsk resident  this is rebel-controlled territory  the enemy is carrying out artillery  shelling and air assaults to strike  positions of our troops says a  spokesperson for ukraine's armed forces  on friday u.s president joe biden  committed to another 150 million dollars  in aid a move rattling russia's nerves  leading to more veiled threats against  the west  and while ukraine's president is eager  for a diplomatic end he says russia  doesn't appear to be willing to engage  but for so many the end came weeks ago  it's a shame to look at this i lived  here for 40 years  72 year old zenita baranchuk lost  everything on march 24th she now lives  in this trailer beside the remains of  her home  i never thought the russian brothers  would attack us and do something like  this with my ukraine she says  meanwhile after a phone call on friday  to underscore a joint commitment in  holding russia accountable both  president biden and prime minister  justin trudeau will join their g7  counterparts for a video conference on  sunday with the invitation extended to  ukraine's president where sanctions are  expected to be on the agenda

